<report>
<title>McNemar and exact (Liddell) test for a paired fourfold table</title>

<p><b>Input table:</b></p>
<table>
<tr><td>@tab_a1</td><td>@tab_b1</td></tr>
<tr><td>@tab_a2</td><td>@tab_b2</td></tr>
</table>

<p>Uncorrected Chi<sub>2</sub> = @{chi:roundu} (1 DF)  <pval>@{chi_p:pval}</pval><br />
Yates' continuity corrected Chi<sub>2</sub> = @{yates_chi:roundu} (1 DF)  <pval>@{yates_chi_p:pval}</pval></p>

<p><b>After Liddell (1983):</b><br />
Point estimate of relative risk (R') = @risk</p>

<p><ci>Exact @pc% confidence interval = @from to @to</ci></p>

<p>F = @{f:roundu}<br />
<pval>Two sided @{tail_2:pval}</pval></p>
<block name="r_prime">

<p><warn>R' is significantly different from unity</warn></p>
</block>
</report>
